// ID: GCI-KQL-LNX-002
// Title: GL.iNet router/KVM Linux persistence and malware-string hunt
// Platform: Microsoft Sentinel
// Type: Triage hunt
// Data source: Syslog (router/Linux syslog forwarding)
// Required fields: TimeGenerated, Computer, HostName, HostIP, ProcessName, SyslogMessage
// Prerequisites: Router syslog forwarding and adequate retention; strings are firmware/campaign-specific.
// Maturity: Draft — validate process/file strings against affected GL.iNet models and firmware
// Source: GL.iNet security notice and BleepingComputer investigation, 2026-11-20/23; https://www.gl-inet.com/en-eu/blogs/blog/glinet-security-notice-2026-11-20
// ATT&CK: T1053.003 — Cron; T1059.004 — Unix Shell (only where process evidence supports the mapping).
// False positives: Legitimate cron jobs, admin scripts, firmware updates and SSH key maintenance.
// Tuning: Correlate with file-integrity monitoring, source IP, process parent, outbound network and approved maintenance.
// Owner: Security Engineering
// Last reviewed: 2026-11-24
// Review by: 2026-12-01

Syslog
| where TimeGenerated >= ago(14d)
| extend Msg = tolower(SyslogMessage)
| where Msg contains "crond -i /tmp/.log"
    or Msg contains "ni.sh"
    or Msg contains "gl-helper"
    or Msg contains "urandom_seed"
    or Msg contains "authorized_keys"
| project TimeGenerated, Computer, HostName, HostIP,
          ProcessName, SyslogMessage
| order by TimeGenerated desc
